{"name":"Cayenne","hex":"#941100","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cayenne","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of French Guiana department, France."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cayenne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cayenne","blocks":[{"text":"Cayenne is the capital, prefecture, and largest city of French Guiana, an overseas region and department of France located in South America. The city stands on a former island at the mouth of the Cayenne River on the Atlantic coast. The city's motto is \"fert aurum industria\", which means \"work brings wealth\". Cayenne is the largest Francophone city of the South American continent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Cayenne_place_des_palmistes_rue_de_Remire_2013.jpg/330px-Cayenne_place_des_palmistes_rue_de_Remire_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayenne"},{"title":"Cayenne (instrumental)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cayenne\" is an instrumental track by the Beatles. It was recorded in 1960, when they were still known as the Quarrymen, and was not officially released until its inclusion on the 1995 album Anthology 1."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayenne_(instrumental)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg/500px-Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg/1280px-Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_co